FreeBSD's fetch(1), ported to OpenBSD.

Retrieves files using HTTP, HTTPS or FTP. Supports HTTP, FTP and SOCKS5
proxies, resuming interrupted transfers and retrying failed requests.

Downloads are written to a temporary file and moved into place only after
successful completion.

TLS is provided by libtls. Uses pledge(2) and unveil(2) to restrict access
to system resources.
